=== Full-grid estimate (1944 configs, 5-fold CV) ===
Sum of one config per patch size : 1084 s
x 648 configs per patch size : 702497 s = 195 GPU-hours

Wall clock by concurrent GPU count:
   2 GPUs :   97.6 h =  4.07 days
   4 GPUs :   48.8 h =  2.03 days
   8 GPUs :   24.4 h =  1.02 days
  16 GPUs :   12.2 h =  0.51 days

Caveat: these three fix projection 64 / 8 heads / depth 4, so they estimate
a mid-cost config in each patch bucket. Configs with depth 6 and projection
128 cost more, those with depth 2 and projection 32 cost less.
The 'worst' config cost 1.31x the p4 mid config, so the true grid
total sits above the figure above. Scale by roughly that factor for a
conservative upper bound: 256 GPU-hours.

Peak GPU memory on the worst config: 1929 MB. This is the
configuration that previously ran out of memory.
